in every war there's always a place  which comes to represent the heart of  the horror and here in ukraine that  place is mariupol  the south eastern port city has been the  site of the heaviest bombardment in this  war homes hospitals schools have all  been hit  the casualty numbers have been hard to  comprehend by the end of the seventh  week the mayor said that twenty thousand  civilians had been killed  they say we have liberated you  from what we had a good life  the city is an urban wasteland but why  is mariupol so important  vladimir putin has been fixated on  taking the city from the outset but the  russian advance has been met with  remarkable ukrainian resistance the  industrial city holds great strategic  and symbolic value for both sides in  this conflict  capturing mariupol is key to moscow's  military campaign and has major  practical value for russia  they want to secure a land corridor  between the donbas and crimea since  russia's invasion and annexation of  crimea in 2014 less than 30 kilometers  has separated mariupol from the  russian-controlled separatist  territories in eastern ukraine  so if russia wants that land corridor  uniting areas of their control they need  to take the city  as the biggest ukrainian city on the sea  of azov mariupol is also a base for the  ukrainian armed forces and is  effectively the only major port serving  the donetsk and luhansk regions of the  donbass controlling mariupol secures  control of the ukrainian coast on the  sea of azov  during russia's invasion they have  targeted both economic and civilian  infrastructure intending to cause as  much damage as possible mariupol is  vital for ukrainian trade too  it's an industrial center for iron and  steel works manufacturing and shipyards  as the largest trading port in the sea  of azov mariupol is also vital for  ukraine's exports including grain coal  iron steel and heavy machinery  russia knows that controlling this key  port as well as it's important to  industries will put huge economic  pressure on ukraine's government  there is symbolism here too to  understand its significance you need to  look back to previous conflicts between  these two countries  russia seized mariupol when they last  invaded ukraine in 2014  but ukraine managed to recapture it  making the city a symbol of ukrainian  resistance for russia for putin mariupol  lies on land that is historically  russian he insists the city is part of  the motherland the territory which now  runs across eastern and southern ukraine  was once known as navaroisia or new  russia after the russian empire took the  region from the ottoman empire in a  series of wars in the 18th century  russia's historic claim to ukrainian  land was for vladimir putin one basic  justification for the invasion he  insisted that although russia lost the  territory its people remained there  mariupol holds significant propaganda  value for russia  when putin launched the invasion of  ukraine on february the 24th he said his  plan was to demilitarize and denazify  ukraine  his claims that ukraine's government are  nazis who have committed genocide are  not true  but it is a narrative that russia has  pushed for years  mariupol plays into this propaganda  because the city is the base for the  azov battalion a nationalist infantry  unit formed in 2014 by volunteers who  share ultra nationalist views  the roots of this unit are far right and  at least in part neo-nazi  the unit has about a thousand members  who were incorporated into ukraine's  national guard they make up just a  fraction of the ukrainian military but  fit russia's nazi narrative  beyond the strategic and symbolic value  control over mariupol is a huge morale  boost to the victor a russian victory in  mariupol enables putin to give the  impression to the russian population  that they are making progress fulfilling  their military goals of liberation from  nazis  for ukraine the loss of mariupol is a  catastrophe for the people whose home it  was  the fall of mariupol also sends a stark  message to other ukrainian cities the  people here have mounted a determined  resistance but at what cost and where  could be next
 

